# Text Elements
Source of threat

(Deadline, danger, negative thought) ^tjTiUDqJ

On the look out for danger


Amygdala hardwired to notice danger and therefore notice the negative in life. ^4hLvfsXo

Alarm Bell Signaled

Amygdala (oldest evolutionary part of our brains, key noticing danger and the fear response, key to survival) sounds alarm bells. ^q4NCFeX0

Emotions heightened

As our awareness of the negative heightened emotional responses intensify. Fear and anger dominate. ^JZOMLjiC

Cortisol triggers brain stem to increase activation of amygdala so it is more vigilant / alert to danger. SNS/HPAA system increased.

Cortisol suppresses hippocampal activity (which inhibits amygdala) so amygdala more alert again.
The cycle continues with greater fuel for the fire. ^ayPCFbcS

Messages Relayed
    The Thalamus (in mid-
brain) sends signals to the brain stem to release norepinephrine or noreadrenalin
(stress hormones) through brain. ^3qGtUjVf

Heart rate increases
Epinephrine increases heart rate so more blood can pump through body, ready for action. Enables pupil to dilate (so draw in more
light –
    
   
  SNS stimulated for action
Stress hormones pump through blood stream. Body prepares to fight or flee.
  
 Pre -
The negativit amygdala, co rational, plannin
frontal Co
rtex inhibited
y / fear bias of
mpromises the
g part of our mind.
           ^OnZ0DFd0

